From eb25234d1cd5a599ff1277998a67542c7d89fd09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry R <rdmitry0911@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:00:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH qemu-server 1/4] fix #4771: vga: add rendernode option for
 virtio-gl

On a host with more than one GPU, a VirGL guest always renders on the
first DRM render node, as QEMU picks it when egl-headless is given
none.  Add a 'rendernode' property to the VGA option, passed on to
egl-headless, so the guest can be placed on a chosen GPU:

  vga: virtio-gl,rendernode=/dev/dri/renderD129

The render node must exist, and the property is refused for other
display types, where it has no effect.

Move the VirGL host checks into assert_virgl_available(), so the new
command lines can be covered by config-to-command tests on a build
host without GL libraries or a GPU.

Signed-off-by: Dmitry R <rdmitry0911@gmail.com>
---
 src/PVE/QemuServer.pm                         | 48 ++++++++++++++-----
 .../cfg2cmd/rendernode-without-virgl.conf     |  5 ++
 src/test/cfg2cmd/virtio-gl-rendernode.conf    |  4 ++
 .../cfg2cmd/virtio-gl-rendernode.conf.cmd     | 34 +++++++++++++
 src/test/cfg2cmd/virtio-gl.conf               |  4 ++
 src/test/cfg2cmd/virtio-gl.conf.cmd           | 34 +++++++++++++
 src/test/run_config2command_tests.pl          |  3 ++
 7 files changed, 121 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/test/cfg2cmd/rendernode-without-virgl.conf
 create mode 100644 src/test/cfg2cmd/virtio-gl-rendernode.conf
 create mode 100644 src/test/cfg2cmd/virtio-gl-rendernode.conf.cmd
 create mode 100644 src/test/cfg2cmd/virtio-gl.conf
